{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794835951521,"sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffewublFfeB69OFwG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e48f2e35001v0S0XbyR84kNeh","sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffewublFfeB69OFwG","messageID":"msg_1e48f1bdf001jQ0rqfmKRkyhta","type":"tool","id":"call_460db77ec5684d9688d8968d","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-188\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy - attach-config-7\n3: description: Review pass seven strategy for the typed command matcher, the advisor vitest config and the guarding tests.\n4: importance_tier: normal\n5: contextType: planning\n6: ---\n7: \n8: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\n9: \n10: ## 2. TOPIC\n11: \n12: Review pass seven of command surfacing, lineage `attach-config-7`. Area files:\n13: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (typed command matcher, including the chained\n14: `:auto`/`:confirm`/`:autopilot`/`:unattended` and `:with-context`/`:with-phases`/`:with-research`\n15: suffix reading), `runtime/vitest.config.ts` (inherited `AI_SESSION_CHILD` cleared, per-run temp\n16: folder), and the tests that pin a child or parent session plus the new boundary and arena-buffer\n17: tests. Diffs are read with `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 85550ee946e 1c3d62def5a -- <path>`.\n18: \n19: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n20: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n21: [All dimensions complete]\n22: \n23: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n24: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n25: \n26: - Not re-scoring stored transcripts or re-running the routing accuracy scorer.\n27: - Not reviewing the scorer's unsafe-verdict logic, the arena builder's production script, or the\n28:   root README; those are the `scorer-7` and `docs-7` areas.\n29: - Not changing code under review. Findings only.\n30: \n31: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n32: \n33: - Convergence at `convergenceThreshold: 0.1`, or `maxIterations: 3`, whichever comes first.\n34: - Any active P0 keeps the verdict at FAIL and the loop continues under the cap.\n35: - No retry of a direction recorded as exhausted in section 10.\n36: \n37: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n38: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n39: - [x] correctness\n40: - [x] security\n41: - [x] traceability\n42: - [x] maintainability\n43: \n44: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n45: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n46: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n47: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n48: - P1 (Required): 0\n49: - P2 (Suggestions): 2\n50: - Resolved: 0\n51: \n52: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n53: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n54: \n55: - Direct diff read plus a reproduction of the changed matcher's exact regexes outside the repository. It proved the positive chain, the unknown-suffix refusal and the boundaries without running the suite or writing outside the lineage. (iteration 1)\n56: - Sweeping every `argument-hint:` line under `.skilled/commands` (46 files) settled the vocabulary question outright: the matcher's set is the complete union, so no missing suffix exists. (iteration 2)\n57: - Reproducing the transcript scorer's `commandParts` split against the same typed input exposed a real downstream parser divergence that a file-local read would have missed. (iteration 2)\n58: \n59: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n60: \n61: - Nothing failed. Running the repository suite was deliberately not attempted: the lineage write surface forbids cache and temp writes outside it, and the behavior under review is pure string matching. (iteration 1)\n62: \n63: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n64: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n65: ### A false `:auto` match inside `:automation`: the negative lookahead rejects the following letter and the chain cannot back down to zero repetitions, which the existing guard test still pins. [SOURCE: .skille