d so the lineage write surface stays inside\n148:   this folder.\n149: \n150: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n151: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n152: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n153: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n154: | `spec_code` | core | pass | 2 | Accepted vocabulary equals the union of all 46 command `argument-hint` documents; no documented suffix refused. |\n155: | `checklist_evidence` | core | notApplicable | 1 | Phase-parent packet has no `checklist.md`; scope is the five area files. |\n156: | `skill_agent` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n157: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n158: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n159: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n160: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n161: \n162: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n163: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n164: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n165: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n166: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` | D1, D3 | 2 | 1 P2 | complete |\n167: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | D1, D3 | 2 | 0 | complete |\n168: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts` | D1 | 1 | 0 | complete |\n169: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/doctor-brief-render.vitest.ts` | D1 | 1 | 0 | complete |\n170: | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-behaviour-guards.vitest.ts` | D1 | 1 | 0 | complete |\n171: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n172: \n173: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n174: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n175: - Max iterations: 3\n176: - Convergence threshold: 0.1\n177: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n178: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n179: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n180: - Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-attach-config-7-1794829999759-g4q8yp, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n181: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n182: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n183: - Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n184: - Severity threshold: P2\n185: - Review target type: spec-folder\n186: - Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n187: - Started: 2026-11-16T12:04:52Z\n188: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-188\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy - attach-config-7\n3: description: Review pass seven strategy for the typed command matcher, the advisor vitest config and the guarding tests.\n4: importance_tier: normal\n5: contextType: planning\n6: ---\n7: \n8: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking\n9: \n10: ## 2. TOPIC\n11: \n12: Review pass seven of command surfacing, lineage `attach-config-7`. Area files:\n13: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` (typed command matcher, including the chained\n14: `:auto`/`:confirm`/`:autopilot`/`:unattended` and `:with-context`/`:with-phases`/`:with-research`\n15: suffix reading), `runtime/vitest.config.ts` (inherited `AI_SESSION_CHILD` cleared, per-run temp\n16: folder), and the tests that pin a child or parent session plus the new boundary and arena-buffer\n17: tests. Diffs are read with `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff 85550ee946e 1c3d62def5a -- <path>`.\n18: \n19: <!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n20: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n21: [All dimensions complete]\n22: \n23: <!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n24: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n25: \n26: - Not re-scoring stored transcripts or re-running the routing accuracy scorer.\n27: - Not reviewing the scorer's unsafe-verdict logic, the arena builder's production script, or the\n28:   root README; those are the `scorer-7` and `docs-7` areas.\n29: - Not changing code under review. Findings only.\n30: \n31: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n32: \n33: - Convergence at `convergenceThreshold: 0.1`, or `maxIterations: 3`, whichever comes first.\n34: - Any active P0 keeps the verdict at FAIL and the loop continues under the cap.\n35: - No retry of a direction recorded as exhausted in section 10.\n36: \n37: <!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n38: ## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n39: - [x] correctness\n40: - [x] security\n41: - [x] traceability\n42: - [x] maintainability\n43: \n44: <!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n45: <!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n46: ## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n47: - P0 (Blockers): 0\n48: - P1 (Required): 0\n49: - P2 (Suggestions): 2\n50: - Resolved: 0\n51: \n52: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n53: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n54: \n55: - Direct diff read plus a reproduction of the changed matcher's exact regexes outside the repository. It proved the positive chain, the unknown-suffix refusal and the boundaries without running the suite or writing outside the lineage. (iteration 1)\n56: - Sweeping every `argument-hint:` line under `.skilled/commands` (46 files) settled the vocabulary question outright: the matcher's set is the complete union, so no missing suffix exists. (iteration 2)\n57: - Reproducing the transcript scorer's `commandParts` split against the same typed input exposed a real downstream parser divergence that a file-local read would have missed. (iteration 2)\n58: \n59: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n60: \n61: - Nothing failed. Running the repository suite was deliberately not attempted: the lineage write surface forbids cache and temp writes outside it, and the behavior under review is pure string matching. (iteration 1)\n62: \n63: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n64: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n65: ### A false `:auto` match inside `:automation`: the negative lookahead rejects the following letter and the chain cannot back down to zero repetitions, which the existing guard test still pins. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:449] -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n66: - What was tried: A false `:auto` match inside `:automation`: the negative lookahead rejects the following letter and the chain cannot back down to zero repetitions, which the existing guard test still pins. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:449]\n67: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n68: - Do NOT retry: A false `:auto` match inside `:automation`: the negative lookahead rejects the following letter and the chain cannot back down to zero repetitions, which the existing guard test still pins. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:449]\n69: \n70: ### A missing documented suffix: the sweep found none; the matcher's set is the complete union. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210] -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n71: - What was tried: A missing documented suffix: the sweep found none; the matcher's set is the complete union. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210]\n72: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n73: - Do NOT retry: A missing documented suffix: the sweep found none; the matcher's set is the complete union. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210]\n74: \n75: ### A per-command vocabulary requirement in the spec: no spec requirement narrows the suffix set per command, so the shared set is not a spec contradiction. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:365] -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n76: - What was tried: A per-command vocabulary requirement in the spec: no spec requirement narrows the suffix set per command, so the shared set is not a spec contradiction. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:365]\n77: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n78: - Do NOT retry: A per-command vocabulary requirement in the spec: no spec requirement narrows the suffix set per command, so the shared set is not a spec contradiction. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:365]\n79: \n80: ### A security regression from the deleted child flag: the deletion is test-process only and production reads the flag at `render.ts:529`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:529] -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n81: - What was tried: A security regression from the deleted child flag: the deletion is test-process only and production reads the flag at `render.ts:529`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:529]\n82: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n83: - Do NOT retry: A security regression from the deleted child flag: the deletion is test-process only and production reads the flag at `render.ts:529`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:529]\n84: \n85: ### A temp-folder exposure: `mkdtempSync` creates the folder owner-only and the exit handler removes it on normal exit. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:17] -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n86: - What was tried: A temp-folder exposure: `mkdtempSync` creates the folder owner-only and the exit handler removes it on normal exit. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:17]\n87: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n88: - Do NOT retry: A temp-folder exposure: `mkdtempSync` creates the folder owner-only and the exit handler removes it on normal exit. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/vitest.config.ts:17]\n89: \n90: ### Catastrophic backtracking: the only new quantifier is `(?::(?:...))+`, each repetition consumes at least one character, and the alternatives are prefix-disambiguated, so the engine backtracks linearly over a prompt-length slice. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210] -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n91: - What was tried: Catastrophic backtracking: the only new quantifier is `(?::(?:...))+`, each repetition consumes at least one character, and the alternatives are prefix-disambiguated, so the engine backtracks linearly over a prompt-length slice. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210]\n92: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n93: - Do NOT retry: Catastrophic backtracking: the only new quantifier is `(?::(?:...))+`, each repetition consumes at least one character, and the alternatives are prefix-disambiguated, so the engine backtracks linearly over a prompt-length slice. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210]\n94: \n95: ### Double reporting the previous review's file-extension limit: not repeated; the recorded limit states the behavior and this iteration found no new input that breaks it. -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n96: - What was tried: Double reporting the previous review's file-extension limit: not repeated; the recorded limit states the behavior and this iteration found no new input that breaks it.\n97: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n98: - Do NOT retry: Double reporting the previous review's file-extension limit: not repeated; the recorded limit states the behavior and this iteration found no new input that breaks it.\n99: \n100: ### Re-reporting the macOS-only `isolation-check.sh` limit or the `started of offered` limit: neither is touched by this area, and no new input breaks them. -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n101: - What was tried: Re-reporting the macOS-only `isolation-check.sh` limit or the `started of offered` limit: neither is touched by this area, and no new input breaks them.\n102: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n103: - Do NOT retry: Re-reporting the macOS-only `isolation-check.sh` limit or the `started of offered` limit: neither is touched by this area, and no new input breaks them.\n104: \n105: ### Regex injection from prompt text: the suffix pattern is a constant and user text is only tested against it; `commandOnlyMentioned` still escapes the command phrase before building its own pattern. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:315] -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n106: - What was tried: Regex injection from prompt text: the suffix pattern is a constant and user text is only tested against it; `commandOnlyMentioned` still escapes the command phrase before building its own pattern. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:315]\n107: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n108: - Do NOT retry: Regex injection from prompt text: the suffix pattern is a constant and user text is only tested against it; `commandOnlyMentioned` still escapes the command phrase before building its own pattern. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:315]\n109: \n110: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n111: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n112: - Completed pivots: 0\n113: - Failed pivots: 0\n114: - Audited overrides: 0\n115: - Swept: none yet\n116: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n117: - Remaining frontier: none rec