The execution-mode suffixes the command docs accept after a slash command,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:41:// either attached (\"/speckit:plan:auto\") or as its own argument (\":auto\").\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:45:const COMMAND_MODE_SUFFIX = /:(?:auto|confirm|autopilot|unattended)(?![\\w-])/gi;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:50:  return prompt.slice(0, command.index) + prompt.slice(command.index).replace(COMMAND_MODE_SUFFIX, ' ');\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:99:// concept: a suffix (\"plan\" -> \"planning\", \"deploy\" -> \"deployment\"). English\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:100:// suffixes start with a vowel or are one of a few consonant-led endings, while a\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:112:  // A doubled final consonant comes before the suffix: \"plan\" -> \"planning\".\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:136:      // A prompt extension (\"regressions\") or a skill word that adds a suffix (\"plan\" -> \"planning\")\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"MODE_SUFFIX\\\\|:auto\\\\|suffix\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794836031203,"end":1794836031792}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794836031800,"sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffewublFfeB69OFwG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4906449002rAlXtwYnO6fWQT","sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffewublFfeB69OFwG","messageID":"msg_1e4901807001jXNHRbdPvwwkIZ","type":"tool","id":"call_4de2f2e66e8143fc8a0da42d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"P2\\|P1\\|P0\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/*.md | head -40"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-001.md:23:### P0 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-001.md:27:### P1 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-001.md:31:### P2 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md:22:### P0 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md:26:### P1 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md:30:### P2 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md:48:   Why it is P2 and not P1: the user-facing attach path is correct, and the defect is confined to how stored runs are scored. It becomes load-bearing only when a recorded run types one of the new suffixes, and then it undercounts rather than misroutes.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md:52:   {\"type\":\"claim\",\"claim\":\"A typed command carrying a :with-* modifier is a different command name for the transcript scorer than for the attach matcher, so a correctly typed chained command is scored as unnamed.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"command-attach.ts:210\",\"command-attach.ts:230\",\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:612\",\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:623\",\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:697\",\"command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:443\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Checked whether commandParts strips every mode suffix before splitting, whether namesCommand compares only the base, and whether the scorer's caller tolerates a longer name. It does not: the exact-equality comparison at line 697 rejects the extra segment.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The divergence may be deliberate if a with-* modifier is treated as command content rather than a suffix. The scorer's own comment calls its pattern the mode suffix, and the command docs classify :with-* as a workflow input on the same command, so a typed command with one is still that command.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade nothing: P2 is already the lowest active tier. If the scorer never reads a stored run with a :with-* suffix, impact is latent, not absent.\"}\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md:92:- Reason: traceability produced one P2 on a measurement surface; the remaining configured dimensions are security and maintainability.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-003.md:22:### P0 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-003.md:26:### P1 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-003.md:30:### P2 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-003.md:40:   Why it is P2 and not P1: the matcher still identifies the command the reader typed, and the per-command parsing belongs to the command, not to the advisor. The defect is the stated scope of the vocabulary, which a follow-on editor would trust and widen further.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-003.md:46:   {\"type\":\"claim\",\"claim\":\"The comment claims per-command documentation drives the accepted suffixes, while the code applies one shared set to commands whose documents advertise no :with-* modifier.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"command-attach.ts:203\",\"command-attach.ts:210\",\"deep/review.md:3\",\"create/sk-skill.md:3\",\"speckit/plan.md:3\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Checked whether another layer narrows the set per command before the suffix is consumed. typedCommandIn and typedCommandForTop both use the same constant, so no layer narrows it.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The shared set may be deliberate, since a modifier that one command documents is harmless on another command. If so, only the comment is wrong, which is the fix the finding names.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"downgradeTrigger\":\"P2 is the lowest active tier. If the command parser rejects an undocumented modifier outright, impact grows to a user-visible misread and this should be raised to P1 on the next pass.\"}\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-003.md:60:| `spec_code` | pass | The accepted set matches the documented union; the per-command scope is recorded as the P2 above rather than as a spec contradiction. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210] |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-003.md:91:- Reason: iteration 3 reaches `maxIterations: 3`; the cap is a legal terminal stop and the remaining findings are P2 advisories.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-003.md:94:- Required evidence: none further; the two P2 findings carry file:line and a concrete input.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-001.md:23:### P0 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-001.md:27:### P1 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-001.md:31:### P2 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md:22:### P0 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md:26:### P1 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md:30:### P2 Findings\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md:48:   Why it is P2 and not P1: the user-facing attach path is correct, and the defect is confined to how stored runs are scored. It becomes load-bearing only when a recorded run types one of the new suffixes, and then it undercounts rather than misroutes.\nspecs/system-skill-advi