ineage reviews only as integration evidence.\n35:    - Affected surface hints: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:612`, `:623`, `:697`\n36:    - Case: a model prints `COMMAND: /speckit:complete:with-research → started` for a row whose expected command is `/speckit:complete`. `commandParts` produces `speckit:complete:with-research`, `namesCommand` compares it with `speckit:complete`, and the mismatch leaves `offerSeen` false even though the command was typed and attached correctly.\n37: \n38:    Reproduction of the scorer's own parser, run outside the repository with the exact source regex and split:\n39: \n40:    ```\n41:    /speckit:complete:auto                 -> {namespace:\"speckit\", name:\"complete\"}                namesExpected=true\n42:    /speckit:complete:with-research        -> {namespace:\"speckit\", name:\"complete:with-research\"}  namesExpected=false\n43:    /speckit:complete:auto:with-research   -> {namespace:\"speckit\", name:\"complete:auto:with-research\"} namesExpected=false\n44:    ```\n45: \n46:    [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:612] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:623] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:697]\n47: \n48:    Why it is P2 and not P1: the user-facing attach path is correct, and the defect is confined to how stored runs are scored. It becomes load-bearing only when a recorded run types one of the new suffixes, and then it undercounts rather than misroutes.\n49: \n50:    Claim adjudication:\n51:    ```json\n52:    {\"type\":\"claim\",\"claim\":\"A typed command carrying a :with-* modifier is a different command name for the transcript scorer than for the attach matcher, so a correctly typed chained command is scored as unnamed.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\"command-attach.ts:210\",\"command-attach.ts:230\",\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:612\",\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:623\",\"score-command-transcripts.mjs:697\",\"command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:443\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Checked whether commandParts strips every mode suffix before splitting, whether namesCommand compares only the base, and whether the scorer's caller tolerates a longer name. It does not: the exact-equality comparison at line 697 rejects the extra segment.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The divergence may be deliberate if a with-* modifier is treated as command content rather than a suffix. The scorer's own comment calls its pattern the mode suffix, and the command docs classify :with-* as a workflow input on the same command, so a typed command with one is still that command.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Downgrade nothing: P2 is already the lowest active tier. If the scorer never reads a stored run with a :with-* suffix, impact is latent, not absent.\"}\n53:    ```\n54: \n55: ## Traceability Checks\n56: \n57: | Protocol | Status | Evidence |\n58: |----------|--------|----------|\n59: | `spec_code` | pass | The accepted vocabulary equals the union of every `argument-hint` suffix under `.skilled/commands`: `:auto` (26 files), `:confirm` (25), `:unattended` (3), `:autopilot` (3), `:with-phases` (2), `:with-context` (2), `:with-research` (1). No documented suffix is refused. [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md:3] [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/speckit/plan.md:3] |\n60: | `checklist_evidence` | notApplicable | Phase-parent packet has no `checklist.md`; scope is the five area files. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:1] |\n61: \n62: The sweep covered every `argument-hint:` line under `.skilled/commands` (46 files), so the comparison is against the whole advertised surface, not a sample.\n63: \n64: ## Integration Evidence\n65: \n66: - `command-attach.ts` is imported by the scorer's fusion path, and both sides name the same typed command there; the drift above is confined to the transcript parser, not to ranking. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1231]\n67: - The scorer's `commandParts` is also used for document lookup and confirm-workflow stems, so the same extra segment affects three read paths, not only `namesCommand`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:645]\n68: - The guard tests pin `/speckit:complete:auto:with-research` as a command for the attach matcher, which is the exact input the scorer still splits differently. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:445]\n69: \n70: ## Edge Cases\n71: \n72: - The scorer's `MODE_SUFFIX` is anchored at the end, so a chain that ends in `:auto` still parses correctly while the same chain ending in `:with-research` does not. The defect is asymmetric, which is why a single path test on `:auto` would not catch it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:612]\n73: - The command docs treat `:with-*` as a workflow input, not an execution mode, which is a reason to keep its words in prompt tokenization. That choice is separate from the name-parsing defect and does not excuse it. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/text.ts:43]\n74: - This finding is reported against the changed matcher line because the transcript parser belongs to the `scorer-7` area. The scorer owner can fix it in its own file; no code was changed here.\n75: \n76: ## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n77: \n78: - Every documented suffix is accepted, and no extra suffix is accepted beyond the documented union. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210]\n79: - The negative cases stay refused: an unknown modifier before or after a known one gives no command. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:447]\n80: - `typedCommandForTop` still gates the command on the leading skill's ownership, so the widened vocabulary cannot carry a command under an unrelated skill. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:261]\n81: \n82: ## Ruled Out\n83: \n84: - A missing documented suffix: the sweep found none; the matcher's set is the complete union. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:210]\n85: - A per-command vocabulary requirement in the spec: no spec requirement narrows the suffix set per command, so the shared set is not a spec contradiction. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:365]\n86: - Double reporting the previous review's file-extension limit: not repeated; the recorded limit states the behavior and this iteration found no new input that breaks it.\n87: \n88: ## Next Focus\n89: \n90: - Dimension: security and maintainability (cross-reference pass)\n91: - Focus area: the vitest config's environment handling as a trust boundary, then the accuracy of the new module comment and the test coverage the branch adds.\n92: - Reason: traceability produced one P2 on a measurement surface; the remaining configured dimensions are security and maintainability.\n93: - Rotation status: correctness and traceability complete; security and maintainability next, in one cross-reference pass because two dimensions remain under a three-iteration cap.\n94: - Blocked/productive carry-forward: direct diff read plus source-reproduced probes stay productive; no blocked approaches.\n95: - Required evidence: an input that crosses the test-environment trust boundary, or a comment claim contradicted by a command document.\n96: - Recovery note: not in recovery.\n97: \n98: Review verdict: PASS"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-7/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794836369051,"end":1794836369267}}}}
