{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794837091179,"sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffewublFfeB69OFwG","part":{"partID":"prt_1e4a08e0b0020oqagxZ34XjSnV","sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffewublFfeB69OFwG","messageID":"msg_1e4a07f88001dfF2JHJrmNwafK","type":"tool","id":"call_00_tazje4gvo1z53fz497zo0xtt","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"plus two pins in the boundary suite (`/speckit:plan:with-phases` and `/deep:review:with-research`, a modifier on a command whose hint omits it).","oldString":"plus two pins in the boundary suite (`/speckit:plan:with-phases` and `/speckit:review`-style `:with-research` on a command whose hint omits it).","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-9/review-report.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-9/review-report.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-9/review-report.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-9/review-report.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-9/review-report.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-9/review-report.md\n@@ -12,9 +12,9 @@\n - **Operator review focus (verbatim)**: \"Review pass nine, lineage attach-config-9. Follow review/review-brief-9.txt and review/review-scope-9.txt: area attach-config covers the typed command matcher's suffix chain in runtime/lib/command-attach.ts, the vitest config that clears an inherited AI_SESSION_CHILD and sets a per-run temp folder, and the tests that pin child or parent sessions. Run the graph and stop steps each iteration, honour the holdout rule, and raise no finding the evidence does not support.\"\n \n ### What was reviewed\n \n-The pass-nine delta for this area is small and precise. Since pass seven the only production change in these four files is the comment over `MODE_SUFFIX` -- rewritten to state that the shared suffix set applies to any tracked command -- plus two pins in the boundary suite (`/speckit:plan:with-phases` and `/speckit:review`-style `:with-research` on a command whose hint omits it). The `:unattended`/`:with-*`/chained-suffix pattern, the `TMPDIR`/`TEMP`/`TMP` export and the `delete process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD` line arrived earlier and were reviewed here at `05f776202e0` because the brief's diff base predates them.\n+The pass-nine delta for this area is small and precise. Since pass seven the only production change in these four files is the comment over `MODE_SUFFIX` -- rewritten to state that the shared suffix set applies to any tracked command -- plus two pins in the boundary suite (`/speckit:plan:with-phases` and `/deep:review:with-research`, a modifier on a command whose hint omits it). The `:unattended`/`:with-*`/chained-suffix pattern, the `TMPDIR`/`TEMP`/`TMP` export and the `delete process.env.AI_SESSION_CHILD` line arrived earlier and were reviewed here at `05f776202e0` because the brief's diff base predates them.\n \n Iteration 1 covered correctness: the chain in every ordinal position, the negative boundaries, case folding, the longest-key rule, the retired-name path, the refusal and question leads, and the deep-loop attach gate. Iteration 2 covered security: the per-run temp folder as a trust boundary, the three-variable export, the exit cleanup and the process-wide child-flag clear, checked against every consumer of `AI_SESSION_CHILD` under the advisor runtime. Iteration 3 covered traceability and maintainability: the accepted vocabulary against all 46 command documents and the packet's own record, then whether the branch's boundary decisions are actually held by tests. Iteration 4 was the confirmation pass that re-read every scope file and reconciled registry, state log and deltas.\n \n ### Why the verdict is PASS\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-9/review-report.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"plus two pins in the boundary suite (`/speckit:plan:with-phases` and `/deep:review:with-research`, a modifier on a command whose hint omits it).\", \"oldString\": \"plus two pins in the boundary suite (`/speckit:plan:with-phases` and `/speckit:review`-style `:with-research` on a command whose hint omits it).\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/attach-config-9/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794837089803,"end":1794837091179}}}}
