{"type":"text","timestamp":1794837199037,"sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffewublFfeB69OFwG","part":{"id":"prt_1e4a224f4001tQ8R5LoXXUxk1G","sessionID":"ses_e1b71e012ffewublFfeB69OFwG","messageID":"msg_1e4a217f500118wRWbWLzsK1C7","type":"text","text":"## Fan-out Lineage Complete — `attach-config-9`\n\n**Stop:** `converged` at iteration 4 of 8 (`all_dimensions_clean`, weighted stop score 0.70, graph `STOP_ALLOWED` with every signal at 1.0). Verdict **PASS**, `hasAdvisories: true`, P0/P1/P2 = 0 / 0 / 1.\n\n**Focus per iteration**\n1. **correctness** — probed the area source directly (the module imports nothing) across the chain's ordinal positions, negatives, case folding, longest-key and retired-name paths, refusal/question leads and the deep-loop gate. Clean.\n2. **security** — treated the vitest config as a trust boundary: owner-only `mkdtemp` folder exported on `TMPDIR`/`TEMP`/`TMP`, exit cleanup, and the process-wide `AI_SESSION_CHILD` clear checked against all 22 references in 8 files. Every child-shape test injects the flag, so the clear weakens no boundary. Clean.\n3. **traceability + maintainability** — accepted vocabulary against all 46 command documents and the packet's D-01/CRIT-4 rows (pass), and the branch's boundary decisions against its tests. One finding.\n4. **confirmation** — re-read every scope file, re-confirmed the P2, reconciled registry/state/deltas/report. No new findings.\n\n**Finding (advisory):** `AC9-P2-001` — the suffix chain's leading anchor is untested. `MODE_SUFFIX` is `^`-anchored, but all four existing negatives fail on the trailing lookahead, so an unanchored variant would pass the suite while accepting `/speckit:complete:draft:auto`. Evidence `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:455`, pattern `command-attach.ts:211`, with the anchored-vs-unanchored reproduction in the iteration.\n\n**State integrity:** 6 state rows (1 run-open + 4 iterations + synthesis), ratios 0/0/1.0/0, graph 12 nodes / 22 edges, registry `COMPLETE` with all four dimensions covered, four deltas (delta 3 carries the finding row), `review-report.md` with all 9 core sections plus the Planning Packet (valid JSON), verdict line exactly once per iteration.\n\n**Two conflicts recorded, not asked:** the brief's \"event line for the convergence decision\" is impossible under the gateway (it accepts only five review events; `deep-review.yaml:955` records the same limit), so the decision rides on the next iteration record and the synthesis event; and the coverage graph is the shared gitignored deep-loop DB written through the brief-mandated `upsert.cjs`. Nothing else was written outside the lineage — the modified `goal.md` and `observability-events.jsonl` are the dispatcher's (`producer: fanout-run`), timestamped outside my run.\n\n**Files written** — all under `specs/.../review/lineages/attach-config-9/`: config, strategy, registry, dashboard, state log (gateway), `review-report.md`, `iterations/iteration-001..004.md`, `deltas/iter-001..004.jsonl`, `.records/` (run-open, four iteration records, synthesis event). No review target, reducer output, command, skill or agent file was touched.\n\n**Yours to do:** the one advisory fix is a single assertion — add `expect(typedCommandIn('/speckit:complete:draft:auto now')).toBeUndefined()` to the unknown-suffix test, naming the leading anchor as the reason.\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:attach-config-9","time":{"start":1794837193972,"end":1794837199037}}}
